========================================================================================
TEST 1 -- MDS errors with CLUSTERED volatility, and a dependent predictor
   log-vol AR(1) at 0.9, phi_x = 0.6.  n = 1000, R = 700, s.e. 0.0082,
   tolerance [0.034, 0.066]
========================================================================================
     theta |   idx 1.5   idx 2.5   idx 4.0
       0.0 |    0.036     0.040     0.050 
       0.5 |    0.046     0.051     0.061 
       1.0 |    0.060     0.054     0.047 
   * outside +-2 s.e.   -> the plug-in survives clustering in BOTH X and eps.

========================================================================================
TEST 2 -- NOT an MDS: serially CORRELATED errors break (MI-t)
   The plug-in Vhat ignores the autocovariances the limit then carries,
   so the size must degrade with rho_e.  This is the theorem's boundary.
========================================================================================
     theta |   rho_e=0.0   rho_e=0.3   rho_e=0.6
       0.0 |      0.041       0.050       0.049 
       1.0 |      0.037       0.053       0.056 
   * outside +-2 s.e.

========================================================================================
TEST 3 -- IS psi-hat_t A MARTINGALE DIFFERENCE ON THE REAL DATA?
   Ljung-Box(10) on each component of psi-hat_t = w_theta(X_t) Y_t X_t
   (H0: beta = 0, so the residual is Y).  chi2(10) 95% = 18.31.
   Also on ||psi||^2, which SHOULD show dependence -- volatility clusters
   even when signs do not, and that is the whole point.
========================================================================================
     Treasury x S&P 500 theta=0.0  median LB   438.01   components rejecting 100.0%   LB(||psi||^2)      865.5
     Treasury x S&P 500 theta=1.0  median LB   197.76   components rejecting 100.0%   LB(||psi||^2)     2713.7
               CP x VIX theta=0.0  median LB    36.46   components rejecting 83.3%   LB(||psi||^2)        8.8
               CP x VIX theta=1.0  median LB    30.23   components rejecting 100.0%   LB(||psi||^2)      716.2

   -> components near the chi2 range with ||psi||^2 far above it is the
      signature the theorem needs: clustered magnitude, unpredictable sign.

